------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party dependencies
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The runtime dependency chain is permissive throughout. Verified against the
installed distribution metadata on 2026-09-21; re-verify before release, since
a licence can change between versions.

  pdfplumber           MIT                          PDF parsing (default)
  pdfminer.six         MIT                          via pdfplumber
  pypdfium2            BSD-3-Clause / Apache-2.0    via pdfplumber
  Pillow               MIT-CMU                      via pdfplumber
  numpy                BSD-3-Clause                 vectors
  faiss-cpu            MIT                          vector index (optional)

Optional, for running the open-weight models:

  torch                BSD-3-Clause
  transformers         Apache-2.0
  accelerate           Apache-2.0
  bitsandbytes         MIT
  sentencepiece        Apache-2.0

Optional, for the Colab notebook's chat interface and OCR (requirements-colab.txt):

  gradio               Apache-2.0                   chat interface (DD-066)
  pytesseract          Apache-2.0                   OCR wrapper (DD-067)
  Tesseract OCR        Apache-2.0                   OCR engine, system package
                                                    (apt-get install tesseract-ocr)

Gradio's own dependency tree is large; its licences were not audited one by one
and it is never imported outside src/chat/ui.py. Verified for the three entries
above against the installed distribution metadata and the Tesseract repository
on 2026-09-24.

Development and test only, NOT a runtime dependency:

  pytest               MIT
  nbformat             BSD-3-Clause                 builds the notebooks (DD-068)
  nbclient             BSD-3-Clause                 executes the notebook in a test
  ipykernel            BSD-3-Clause                 the kernel nbclient runs
  PyMuPDF              AGPL-3.0 or commercial

PyMuPDF is deliberately excluded from the runtime dependencies. It is used only
to write the synthetic PDFs the test suite builds, and as an alternative parser
backend for anyone who accepts AGPL terms. Installing this project does not
install it. See DD-033 in DESIGN_DECISIONS.md.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Model weights
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Model weights are downloaded at runtime and are NOT covered by this project's
licence. Their terms are their own and must be checked per checkpoint, not
inferred from the vendor (DD-024):

  Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507      Apache-2.0      default generator
  Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct       Apache-2.0      low-memory preset
  Qwen/Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct         qwen-research   NON-COMMERCIAL, not a default
  BAAI/bge-m3                      MIT             embeddings
  BAAI/bge-reranker-v2-m3          Apache-2.0      reranking (Phase 4)

Verified against the Hugging Face model cards on 2026-09-20. The configuration
layer refuses to make a non-commercially-licensed checkpoint the default
generator unless the caller explicitly opts in.

